# ── Monitor layout ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auto-arrange every output at its native mode; an external monitor extends to
# the right by default. This file is machine-local (gitignored, seeded from this
# .default by install.sh) and is rewritten by the GUI (nwg-displays) or by hand.
#
# Manual examples:
#   monitor = eDP-2,    1920x1080@144, 0x0,    1
#   monitor = HDMI-A-1, preferred,     1920x0, 1              # extend right
#   monitor = HDMI-A-1, preferred,     0x0,    1, transform,1 # portrait (90°)
#   monitor = HDMI-A-1, preferred,     auto,   1, mirror, eDP-2
#
# Quick presets without editing this file: SUPER+O  (or monitor.sh …).
monitor = , preferred, auto, 1
